+	                                         ///< false: a resizable window on the Workbench screen, sharing its palette.
+	                                         ///< DEFAULTS TO TRUE, and that default is the upgrade guarantee: OpenTTD's own
+	                                         ///< "fullscreen" setting defaults to false and is already written in every
+	                                         ///< existing openttd.cfg, so hanging window mode off THAT would have moved every
+	                                         ///< current player into a window on upgrade. A new key cannot be in an old
+	                                         ///< config, so an old config keeps the behaviour it has.
+	uint16 win_w, win_h;                     ///< last size of the Workbench window, in pixels. Written by the video
+	                                         ///< driver, never by the player - exactly like amiga.rtg below. It exists
+	                                         ///< because a dragged window size is NOT a screen mode: putting it in
+	                                         ///< _cur_resolution (which is what openttd.cfg records for the display)
+	                                         ///< left the next start hunting for "618x247" in the resolution list,
+	                                         ///< failing, and dropping to 320x256. Zero means "no window size yet".
