+	                                         ///< port has always done. Turning it OFF skips the startup scan and refuses to
+	                                         ///< load anything from the [newgrf] section, which is the only way to get that
+	                                         ///< memory back on a 24 MB machine - once a GRF is in the sprite cache it stays.
+	                                         ///< Read at startup, so a change needs a restart; the setting proc says so.
+	byte   music_source;                     ///< where the music comes from: 0 = the sampled WAV set in music/ played
+	                                         ///< through Paula (the default, and what every release so far has done),
+	                                         ///< 1 = the OpenMSX MIDI set we ship in gm/, 2 = the player's own original
+	                                         ///< Transport Tycoon Deluxe .gm files, also in gm/. We may not distribute
+	                                         ///< those, so 2 does nothing until the player copies them in themselves.
+	                                         ///< Both MIDI modes need camd.library and a MIDI device routed to "out.0";
+	                                         ///< without one the driver says so in the log and plays the sampled set.
+	                                         ///< Read while the base sets are scanned, i.e. before the music driver even
+	                                         ///< starts, so a change needs a restart - the setting text says as much.
+	byte   midi_out;                         ///< where MIDI notes leave the machine: 0 = try camd.library and fall
+	                                         ///< back to the serial port, 1 = camd.library only, 2 = raw MIDI on
+	                                         ///< serial.device at 31250 baud only. The serial route exists because
+	                                         ///< CAMD can succeed and still be silent - with the library installed
+	                                         ///< but no driver in DEVS:midi, every note falls into an empty cluster -
+	                                         ///< and because a plain MIDI interface on the serial port needs no CAMD
