+	                                         ///< requests, not the bytes: a reporter measured 3:50 from PFS and 2:20
+	                                         ///< from FFS against 0:50 from a RAM disk, while COPYING the whole game
+	                                         ///< to that RAM disk took 16 seconds. Reading each file once, in one go,
+	                                         ///< is what closes that gap. Costs about 16 MB. Default TRUE, but it is
+	                                         ///< switched off by itself at startup when there is not enough free Fast
+	                                         ///< RAM, so a 24 MB machine keeps working without the player deciding
+	                                         ///< anything. Read once, at the first file open, so a change needs a restart.
+	bool   wb_bar;                           ///< keep the system screen title bar visible (flip to Workbench); costs game area
+	bool   hide_game_pointer;                ///< hide OpenTTD's own SOFTWARE cursor; the Intuition system pointer stays visible
